+## Shakedown findings — this leg (non-binding, binding intent lives in the specs)
+
+Two further browser-only acceptance defects, pinned as new scenarios on `watchbill.json`:
+
+- **List re-render detaches nodes (acceptance: Mark all as completed; Item mark/unmark
+  complete).** Every state change calls `render()`, which does `list.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds
+  all `<li>` nodes. A real browser keeps the pre-click node reference, so Cypress's chain after
+  the click fails (`cy.eq`/`cy.find` on a detached node). The happy-dom harness re-queries fresh
+  each time, which is why the existing toggle scenarios passed; a node captured before the click
+  and re-checked for attachment after reproduces the detach. Pins:
+  - `features/todomvc.feature:Toggling a todo preserves its list item node`
+  - `features/todomvc.feature:Toggling all preserves every list item node`
+  Crew fix: mutate the existing `<li>`/checkbox in place (toggle `completed` class and
+  `checked`) instead of rebuilding the list. The scenarios redden on current code.
+- **Editing does not hide other controls (acceptance: Editing, hide other controls when
+  editing).** `index.html` links no stylesheet, so `node_modules/todomvc-app-css/index.css`
+  (which carries `.todo-list li.editing .view { display: none }`) never loads and `.toggle`
+  stays visible in edit mode. happy-dom cannot compute CSS visibility, so this is guarded at the
+  source level by a `@contract` page-reference pin:
+  - `features/todomvc.feature:The served page links the application stylesheet`
+  Crew fix: add the stylesheet `<link>` to `index.html` (CSS chain per build intent:
+  `todomvc-common/base.css`, `todomvc-app-css/index.css`, then `css/app.css`).
+
